Hi Matt and JBP,

The weights problem is easy -- weights should not be quoted! The
proper specification is

obj <- zelig(treat~black+married, model = "poisson",  robust=TRUE,
weights=w,data = lalonde, cite=FALSE)
summary(obj)

The robust option does not seem to work at all 4.1-0 (I haven't rolled
back to 3.5 to check it there):

all.equal(summary(obj1)$coefficients, summary(obj2)$coefficients,
summary(obj2)$coefficients)
#[1] TRUE

Finally version 4.1-0 doesn't average runs on multiply data
imputations (see e.g.,
http://comments.gmane.org/gmane.comp.lang.r.zelig/846) so again I
haven't rolled back to 3.5 to see if this works. But JBP, if you're
using 3.5 it could be as simple as removing the quotes around the
weights = "w" argument.

HTH,
Ista

